# Mormon Bridge - Web + Capacitor Project Rules

## Language and Framework
- This is a TypeScript + React + Vite project wrapped with Capacitor for mobile
- Always use TypeScript (not plain JS) for all source files under `web/src/`
- Refer to the React, Vite, Vitest, and Capacitor docs when implementing features
- Follow React best practices: hooks, functional components, composition over inheritance

## Code Style
- Use 2 SPACES for indentation in all `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.css`, and config files
- Follow TypeScript/React naming conventions:
  - camelCase for variables and functions
  - PascalCase for React components, types, and interfaces
  - SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for constants
  - kebab-case for file names (e.g. `game-rules.ts`, `card-hand.tsx`)
- Prefer named exports over default exports (except React components which may use default)
- Use ASCII characters for quotes, dashes, and punctuation (use " and ' not " " ' ')

## Architecture rules
- `web/src/game/` is a PURE TypeScript module — no React, no DOM, no Capacitor imports allowed here
- All game state is a plain serializable object (`GameState`); never mutate it in place
- Game moves are pure functions: `(state: GameState, action: Action) => GameState`
- `web/src/ui/` contains React components that render game state and dispatch actions
- `web/src/app/` contains top-level screens (menu, local game, settings)
- Tests live alongside source files as `*.test.ts` and run via `npm test` (Vitest)

## Resources
- React: https://react.dev/
- Vite: https://vitejs.dev/
- Vitest: https://vitest.dev/
- Capacitor: https://capacitorjs.com/docs
- TypeScript: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/
